---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

// Local SEO without doorway pages.
//
// The obvious build here is one page per city, differing only by name. That
// is the scaled-content pattern Google penalises, and it would be dishonest
// besides: this is a Zoom practice with no office in Naples.
//
// Instead: one substantive page, with per-county sections carrying facts that
// genuinely differ. The circuits really do run different programs, with
// different income thresholds and different local requirements, and that
// difference is the honest reason a private mediator exists.
//
// COMPLIANCE, and the reason this page is framed the way it is: the Florida
// Supreme Court family mediator certification is PENDING. Court-referred
// family mediation requires it. So nothing here may suggest this practice
// takes court-ordered work. Every section describes the court's own program
// as the court's, and this practice as the private, voluntary alternative
// that parties choose together. When the certification is approved, these
// sections can gain a court-referred paragraph. Not before.

const counties = [
  {
    name: "Palm Beach County",
    circuit: "Fifteenth Judicial Circuit",
    seat: "West Palm Beach",
    court:
      "The circuit runs its own family mediation program using staff mediators, for dissolution, paternity and custody cases where the parties' combined income is up to $100,000. Its published fees are $60 per person per session below $50,000 combined, and $120 per person between $50,000 and $100,000.",
    note:
      "This is the home county. The office address on the Contact page is here, though sessions are still held over Zoom.",
  },
  {
    name: "Broward County",
    circuit: "Seventeenth Judicial Circuit",
    seat: "Fort Lauderdale",
    court:
      "The circuit's family mediation program requires that the case already be filed in Broward and that a Broward judge has signed a family mediation order. It is subject to a legislative income limit, described by the circuit as combined net income under $100,000.",
    note:
      "Because the program needs a filed case and a signed order, it is not available to a couple who have not filed yet.",
  },
  {
    name: "Miami-Dade County",
    circuit: "Eleventh Judicial Circuit",
    seat: "Miami",
    court:
      "Miami-Dade treats mediation as a step to be completed before a dissolution case can be set for trial. The circuit operates its own Mediation and Arbitration Division for court-referred matters.",
    note:
      "Couples here often reach agreement privately first, then file, rather than waiting for the court to refer them.",
  },
  {
    name: "Martin and St. Lucie Counties",
    circuit: "Nineteenth Judicial Circuit",
    seat: "Stuart and Fort Pierce",
    court:
      "The Treasure Coast circuit covers Martin, St. Lucie, Indian River and Okeechobee counties, and operates its own alternative dispute resolution programs for filed cases.",
    note:
      "A largely rural circuit where travel to the courthouse is a real cost, which is part of why remote sessions suit it.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Areas Served in Florida · Pro Se Fair Play Mediation"
  description="Private mediation for Palm Beach, Broward, Miami-Dade, Martin and St. Lucie counties and the rest of Florida. How each circuit's court program differs, and where private mediation fits."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    name: "Private Mediation in Florida",
    serviceType: "Private Mediation",
    description:
      "Voluntary private mediation, held over Zoom, for parties anywhere in Florida who choose to resolve matters without a court referral.",
    url: "https://prosefairplaymediation.com/areas-served",
    provider: {
      "@type": "ProfessionalService",
      name: "Pro Se Fair Play Mediation, LLC",
      url: "https://prosefairplaymediation.com",
      telephone: "+1-561-941-0896",
    },
    areaServed: [
      { "@type": "State", name: "Florida" },
      ...counties.map((c) => ({ "@type": "AdministrativeArea", name: `${c.name}, Florida` })),
    ],
    availableChannel: {
      "@type": "ServiceChannel",
      name: "Online via Zoom",
      serviceUrl: "https://prosefairplaymediation.com/book",
    },
  })} />

  <header class="areas-header">
    <div class="container areas-header-inner">
      <Breadcrumbs trail={[]} current="Areas Served" tone="light" />
      <p class="kicker">
        <span class="kicker-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Where I Work
      </p>
      <h1 class="display areas-title">
        Serving Florida<span class="display-italic">, by Zoom</span><span class="display-italic">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede areas-lede">
        Sessions are held online, so where you live in Florida does not limit
        whether we can work together. What does differ by county is how the
        local court handles mediation, and that is worth understanding before
        you decide how to proceed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="areas-intro">
    <div class="container-narrow areas-prose">
      <h2>Private mediation, not court-referred</h2>
      <p>
        There are two routes to a mediated agreement in Florida, and they are
        not the same thing.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first is <strong>court-referred mediation</strong>. A case has
        already been filed, a judge orders the parties to mediate, and the
        circuit's own program handles it. Each circuit below runs one, and each
        sets its own rules and income limits.
      </p>
      <p>
        The second is <strong>private mediation</strong>, chosen voluntarily by
        both parties. It does not require a filed case, a judge's order, or the
        court's involvement at all. Parties often use it before filing, so that
        what they eventually file is uncontested. <strong>That is the service
        offered here.</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="areas-callout">
        <p>
          One practical consequence worth knowing: several circuits limit their
          staff mediation programs to households under roughly $100,000 in
          combined income. Couples above that threshold are generally not
          eligible for the court's own mediators and arrange private mediation
          instead.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Whether mediation is required in your particular case, and which
        programs you qualify for, are questions for the court where your case
        would be filed or for an attorney who represents you. The summaries
        below describe each circuit's published program, not your situation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="areas-list-section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2 class="areas-h2">County by county</h2>
      <ul class="areas-list" role="list">
        {counties.map((c) => (
          <li class="area">
            <div class="area-head">
              <h3 class="area-name display">{c.name}</h3>
              <p class="area-circuit smallcaps">{c.circuit}</p>
            </div>
            <p class="area-seat">Courthouse seat: {c.seat}</p>
            <p class="area-court">{c.court}</p>
            <p class="area-note">{c.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="areas-prose areas-rest">
        <h2>Everywhere else in Florida</h2>
        <p>
          Florida has twenty judicial circuits, and the four above are simply
          the ones that come up most often here. Private mediation is not tied
          to a circuit: if both parties agree to mediate, they can do so from
          anywhere in the state, and the session runs over Zoom regardless.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are outside these counties and want to know how your local
          court handles mediation,{" "}
          <a class="link-underline" href="/contact">get in touch</a> and I will
          point you at that circuit's published information, or{" "}
          <a class="link-underline" href="/book">book a free consultation</a>{" "}
          and we can talk it through.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="areas-cta">
    <div class="container-narrow areas-cta-inner">
      <a class="btn btn-primary areas-cta-btn" href="/book">
        Book a Free, Private Consultation
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .areas-header {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 6vw + 2rem, 7rem) clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 22% 28%, rgba(196, 154, 75, 0.09), transparent 55%),
      var(--color-cream);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .areas-header-inner { position: relative; max-width: 64rem; }
  .areas-title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    font-weight: 400;
    max-width: 20ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .areas-title .display-italic { color: var(--color-gold-deep); }
  .areas-lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 60ch; color: var(--color-ink-soft); }

  .areas-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
    background: var(--color-cream-warm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }
  .areas-prose {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .areas-prose p { max-width: 64ch; }
  .areas-prose p + p { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .areas-prose strong { color: var(--color-navy); font-weight: 600; }
  .areas-prose h2,
  .areas-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .areas-prose h2 + p { margin-top: 0; }

  .areas-callout {
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.35rem;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
    border-radius: 0 3px 3px 0;
  }
  .areas-callout p { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; }

  .areas-list-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-3xl);
    background: var(--color-cream);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }
  .areas-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xl); display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .area {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }
  .area:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider); }
  .area-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .area-name {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .area-circuit {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--color-gold-deep);
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .area-seat,
  .area-court,
  .area-note {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .area-seat {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-slate);
  }
  .area-court { margin-top: 0.7rem; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--color-ink-soft); }
  .area-note {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-slate);
  }

  .areas-rest { margin-top: var(--space-xl); }

  .areas-cta {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--color-cream-warm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }
  .areas-cta::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--color-gold) 40%, var(--color-gold) 60%, transparent);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .areas-cta-inner { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .areas-cta-btn {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    border-color: var(--color-navy);
  }
  .areas-cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-navy-deep);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    border-color: var(--color-gold);
  }
</style>
